    "category": "Non-automatic weighing instrument (scanner/scale)",
    "type_designations": ["Magellan 9300i", "Magellan 9400i", "939404", "939406"],
    "module_designation": "Not applicable",
    "description": "Class III, mains operated, self-indicating, weight only, single or dual interval Non-Automatic Weighing Instrument designed for direct sales to the public. The diecast base unit supports the load cell, barcode scanner assembly, main board and analogue boards; the scale sub-assembly is mounted on the load cell and the steel 'L' shaped load receptor is mounted on the four supporting points. Designed to be flush-mounted in a fixed position in a checkout surface; may be fitted with a level indicator. Devices: initial zero setting device, semi-automatic zero setting device, zero tracking device, automatic zero setting device, zero indicator, gravity compensation. Interfaces: POS terminal (RJ10), remote display (RJ4), scale host (RJ10), auxiliary port (RJ10), EAS port (RJ45), power (Molex 3 pin), USB, image port. Markings: Max, Min, e=, accuracy class, serial number, manufacturer's mark or name, certificate number, special temperature limits (+10 °C to +40 °C); labels affixed on the sub platter underneath the load receptor. Legally relevant parameters (scale configuration and calibration) stored in EEPROM with software version numbers 1-70-28 and 2-0-0; access to calibration mode only by operating a switch behind a sealing cap; EEPROM, calibration switch and load cell secured by a tamper-evident solution bearing a securing mark."
